[TEXT] Key findings:

**dswa1 full rules:**
```
-P FORWARD ACCEPT
-A FORWARD -s 10.1.0.0/24 -d 10.3.0.0/24 -i br0.10 -p icmp -j ACCEPT
-A FORWARD -s 10.1.0.0/24 -d 10.3.0.0/24 -i br0.10 -j DROP
```

ICMP explicitly ACCEPT-ed then everything else DROP-ped for Office A→B. This allows ping (masking the fault) but blocks all TCP.

**curl from pc3:**
- `http://10.1.0.100` → EXIT:28 (timeout) — TCP SYN-ACK dropped by dswa rule
- `http://10.5.0.4` (srv1) → EXIT:7 (connection refused) — no web server on srv1

Real symptoms confirmed on both fronts. Check dswa2 rules and srv1 web service state, then pivot to ACL-skill:
