[TEXT] dswa2 has identical rules to dswa1. srv1 has zero web server processes (apache, nginx, httpd all absent).

Full picture confirmed:
- **dswa1/dswa2**: `ACCEPT icmp` + `DROP all` for 10.1.0.0/24→10.3.0.0/24 on br0.10 — allows ping (hides fault) but drops all TCP SYN-ACK replies, causing pc3 → Office A TCP to time out (EXIT:28)
- **srv1**: No web server running → EXIT:7 connection refused for HTTP

The dswa ACL is the primary injected fault matching acl-skill: selective protocol drop. Both distribution switches have identical rules (coordinated maintenance change). The ICMP ACCEPT before DROP specifically deceives ping-based testing.

